			<div class="py-5"></div>
			<div class="my-2"></div>
			<div class="row my-3 g-3 align-items-stretch">
				<div class="col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 d-flex flex-column">
					<div class="card-wysiwyg-body d-flex flex-column h-100 w-100 flex-fill rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-area text-dark">
<h6>Utility Assistance</h6>
<p>Millions of people across the country are forced into making a choice between things like being able to keep the lights on or put food on their family's table.</p>
<p>We believe no one should have to make a decision like that, so we provide utility assistance and relief to those who need it. We have always fought to ensure that no one goes without heat in the coldest winters, air conditioning in the brutal summers or fresh water to drink and bathe in.</p>
</div>
				</div>
				<div class="col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 d-flex flex-column">
					<div class="card-wysiwyg-body d-flex flex-column h-100 w-100 flex-fill rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-area text-dark">
<h6>Emergency Shelter</h6>
<p>2 W grace street: Serving single men and families who are experiencing homelessnes.</p>
<p>1900 Chamberlayne avenue: Serving single men who are experiencing homelessness.</p>
<p>If you are within 3 days of experiencing homelessness, please contact the Homeless Connection Line at <a href="tel:8049720813">804-972-0813</a>.</p>
</div>
				</div>
				<div class="col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 d-flex flex-column">
					<div class="card-wysiwyg-body d-flex flex-column h-100 w-100 flex-fill rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-area text-dark">
<h6>Case Management</h6>
<p>Our case managers concentrate on helping residents identify problems that may have contributed to their homelessness, including substance abuse, employment, education deficiencies, financial mismanagement and mental health.</p>
<p>Staff assist each resident in developing realistic goals to overcome their situations. Substance abuse, motivational, and ‘Life Skills Enrichment’ meetings are conducted weekly at the shelter.</p>
</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="my-2"></div>
			<div class="row my-3 g-3 align-items-stretch">
				<div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 d-flex flex-column">
					<div class="card-wysiwyg-body d-flex flex-column h-100 w-100 flex-fill rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-area text-dark">
<h6>Refereral Services</h6>
<p>We provide referral services as part of our broader community services. This includes connecting individuals and families with resources for various needs, such as housing, food, financial assistance and educational opportunities.</p>
</div>
				</div>
				<div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 d-flex flex-column">
					<div class="card-wysiwyg-body d-flex flex-column h-100 w-100 flex-fill rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-area text-dark">
<h6>Building wealth &amp; health network</h6>
<p>This a free, 16-session curriculum over eight weeks, promoting financial literacy and self empowerment.</p>
<p>Participation is limited to Richmond City residents who care for one or more children, 18-years or younger.</p>
<p>To learn more about the Network and register for one of two informations sessions, visit our events page and click on "Building Wealth and Health Network - Cohort 3."</p>
</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row my-3 g-3 align-items-stretch">
				<div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6 col-sm-12">
					<div class="card-wysiwyg-body d-flex flex-column h-100 w-100 flex-fill rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-area text-dark">
<h6>Homeless Connection Line</h6>
<p>If you are within 3 days of losing housing, contact the Homeless Crisis Line for support. The Homeless Connection Line (HCL) is managed by Homeward and is a crucial community resource for those experiencing homelessness or within a few days of losing their current housing. The HCL offers trained Diversion Specialists who can assist households within 3 days of losing their housing to problem-solve, access community resources, and connect to homeless assistance if needed.</p>
<p>The Central Intake System is managed by <a href="http://www.homewardva.org" target="">Homeward</a>. They are the first point of entry into shelter services.</p>
<p><em>Homeless Connection Line Intake: <a href="tel:8049720813" target="">804.972.0813</a></em></p>
<ul>
<li>Weekdays: 8:00 a.m. - 9:00 p.m.</li>
<li>Weekends: 1:00 - 9:00 p.m.</li>
</ul>
</div>
				</div>
				<div class="col-lg-6 col-md-6 col-sm-12">
					<div class="card-wysiwyg-body d-flex flex-column h-100 w-100 flex-fill rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-area text-dark" style="color: #ed1c2b;">
<h6>Chamberlayne Avenue Emergency Shelter</h6>
<p>1900 Chamberlayne Avenue, Richmond, VA 23222</p>
<p><strong>Men's Emergency Shelter</strong></p>
<p><em>Homeless Connection Line Intake: <a href="tel:8049720813" target="">804.972.0813</a></em></p>
<p><strong>Inclement Weather Shelter</strong></p>
<ul>
